            <ArticleTitle>[Crossed renal ectopy with fusion. Report of a case].</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>131-3</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Crossed renal ectopia is a rare urinary tract anomaly, often associated with malformations involving various organs and systems. We report a case of crossed renal ectopy with fusion, without associated abnormalities. Recurrent abdominal pain, sometimes with microhematuria, were the clinical features, never accompanied by alteration of the renal function.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
